WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:00:02.390 --> 00:00:05.990
[LUFFY]
So Robin is in that
building behind you, huh?

3
00:00:06.890 --> 00:00:08.820
Outta my way, bull guy!

4
00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:10.710
[BLUENO]
Listen boy.

5
00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:14.740
Perhaps you haven't realized this
but what you are doing right now

6
00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:17.840
is nothing short of
a world-class crime.

7
00:02:15.370 --> 00:02:18.080
[MARINE]
Bring down every last one of them!

8
00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:21.790
[ZAMBAI]
Keep firing! Send those marines packing!

9
00:02:21.830 --> 00:02:26.210
<b>Signal the Counterstrike</b>

10
00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:31.590
[SANJI]
Stupid bastards!

11
00:02:43.790 --> 00:02:46.230
So then, when Sodom
and his brother Gomorrah

12
00:02:46.230 --> 00:02:50.630
were about to die in the belly of a Sea
King, the Franky Family showed up!

13
00:02:50.630 --> 00:02:54.200
They were rescued and told these
fateful words that he still remembers:

14
00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:57.540
"Look, we're already full
so we're not gonna eat you!"

15
00:02:57.540 --> 00:02:59.710
And from that day forward,
the two brothers swore

16
00:02:59.710 --> 00:03:02.880
their undying loyalty
to their savior, Franky.

17
00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:06.020
[SANJI]
So let me get this straight.

18
00:03:06.020 --> 00:03:08.820
The Franky Family brought
down a Sea King, ate it,

19
00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:12.890
and they just happened to be saved
because Franky was already full?

20
00:03:12.890 --> 00:03:14.730
[NAMI]
Pretty much.

21
00:03:14.730 --> 00:03:15.430
Fine.

22
00:03:15.430 --> 00:03:16.640
Whatever.

23
00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:17.780
You mind watching where you're going?

24
00:03:17.780 --> 00:03:19.410
You're making me nervous.

25
00:03:21.110 --> 00:03:25.420
[CHOPPER]
"I will follow Big Bro Franky
until the day I die!" he says.

26
00:03:25.850 --> 00:03:30.320
[SANJI]
I bet he's really happy that one
of us can understand what he's saying.

27
00:03:38.190 --> 00:03:40.330
[CHOPPER]
He said "By the way, the masked guy

28
00:03:40.330 --> 00:03:42.400
that was with you never
made it on board my back.

29
00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:43.730
Is that okay?"

30
00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:51.670
He's talking about Sniper King!

31
00:03:51.670 --> 00:03:53.800
Where is he?

32
00:03:54.770 --> 00:03:57.090
Why now? Why now?

33
00:03:57.090 --> 00:03:57.920
Idiot.

34
00:03:57.920 --> 00:03:59.120
Did he fall off?

35
00:03:59.120 --> 00:03:59.960
Didn't you hear?

36
00:03:59.960 --> 00:04:02.060
He hasn't been here from the start!

37
00:04:02.060 --> 00:04:03.090
Don't tell me.

38
00:04:03.090 --> 00:04:04.760
Did he run away again?

39
00:04:04.930 --> 00:04:09.400
<b>Courthouse</b>
<b>Island Gate</b>

40
00:04:09.440 --> 00:04:11.770
<b>Galley-La vs. the Courthouse Guard Force</b>

41
00:04:12.160 --> 00:04:13.460
Arrogant pirates!

42
00:04:13.460 --> 00:04:16.030
You can't keep this
foolishness up forever!

43
00:04:16.810 --> 00:04:19.660
[LULU]
If you wanna pass, you'll have
to go through me to do it!

44
00:04:19.660 --> 00:04:21.520
Fine then!

45
00:04:21.520 --> 00:04:23.630
Attack!

46
00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:29.470
[LULU]
Is that really the best you've got?

47
00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:31.930
[TILESTONE]
Battleship Cannon!

48
00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:37.340
Come on!

49
00:04:37.340 --> 00:04:38.500
There's only three of them!

50
00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:40.000
Do something!

51
00:04:41.950 --> 00:04:45.850
[PAULIE]
So, you're good at
fighting, aren't you?

52
00:04:46.650 --> 00:04:49.490
Then you can beat those guys, huh?

53
00:04:49.490 --> 00:04:50.960
You bet.

54
00:04:56.210 --> 00:04:57.240
[PAULIE]
We'll get her back.

55
00:04:57.240 --> 00:04:59.340
We just needed motivation.

56
00:05:00.040 --> 00:05:03.580
Now that we know Robin needs saving,
there's no limit to what Luffy

57
00:05:03.580 --> 00:05:06.020
and the rest of our
crew can accomplish!

58
00:05:07.470 --> 00:05:08.970
[PAULIE]
I believe in him.

59
00:05:08.970 --> 00:05:10.340
He can do it.

60
00:05:10.770 --> 00:05:11.470
Go!

61
00:05:11.470 --> 00:05:13.310
Get that rope guy!

62
00:05:14.940 --> 00:05:16.610
Not gonna happen!

63
00:05:17.390 --> 00:05:21.060
Shrouds and Ratline Knot!

64
00:05:21.060 --> 00:05:23.520
We're done for!

65
00:05:24.210 --> 00:05:26.060
Consider this a dead end.

66
00:05:26.060 --> 00:05:27.260
Give up and go.

67
00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:36.770
Just get to the point already.

68
00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:41.540
The power of the World
Government stretches across

69
00:05:41.540 --> 00:05:44.750
more than one hundred
and seventy nations.

70
00:05:44.750 --> 00:05:48.250
This island is a symbol
of our strength and resolve.

71
00:05:48.250 --> 00:05:51.350
Attacking it is not simply
an act of rebellion,

72
00:05:51.350 --> 00:05:55.760
but a declaration of war against
every country in our alliance.

73
00:05:55.760 --> 00:05:58.970
We are bound by our
honor to strike you down.

74
00:05:58.970 --> 00:06:01.440
[BLUENO]
You will not only
face a merciless death,

75
00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:04.440
but serve as an example
to the entire world.

76
00:06:04.440 --> 00:06:07.250
You're, at most, a few dozen men.

77
00:06:07.870 --> 00:06:10.530
You should have thought
this out more carefully.

78
00:06:10.530 --> 00:06:12.900
I said "outta my way."

79
00:06:12.900 --> 00:06:14.540
So you gonna move, or what?

80
00:06:14.540 --> 00:06:16.540
It doesn't matter if I move or not.

81
00:06:16.540 --> 00:06:17.780
The point is that
you condemned yourself

82
00:06:17.780 --> 00:06:21.450
to a death sentence the second
you set foot on Enies Lobby.

83
00:06:21.450 --> 00:06:22.880
You understand that?

84
00:06:22.880 --> 00:06:24.650
Fighting is a waste of time.

85
00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:27.800
You got a taste of our
strength at Iceberg's mansion.

86
00:06:27.800 --> 00:06:31.100
You cannot defeat our Six Powers.

87
00:06:31.100 --> 00:06:33.970
The difference between
us is simply too great.

88
00:06:36.840 --> 00:06:38.640
[LUFFY]
Yeah, maybe that's true.

89
00:06:38.640 --> 00:06:43.350
But y'know, for some reason, I have
a feeling I'm gonna win this time!

90
00:06:46.540 --> 00:06:48.110
[LUFFY]
Here we go!

91
00:06:49.540 --> 00:06:50.850
[BLUENO]
Iron Body.

92
00:06:50.850 --> 00:06:52.960
[LUFFY]
Gum-Gum Rifle!

93
00:07:04.730 --> 00:07:05.870
[BLUENO]
This doesn't make any sense!

94
00:07:05.870 --> 00:07:08.840
He wasn't like this at all
when I fought him before!

95
00:07:08.840 --> 00:07:11.440
How is it that he's so
much stronger now?

96
00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:14.160
[LUFFY]
Gatling!

97
00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:15.160
[BLUENO]
Shave!

98
00:07:43.890 --> 00:07:47.560
[LUFFY]
I don't care about your honor,
or your Government, or any of that.

99
00:07:47.560 --> 00:07:50.000
You do what you want with that crap.

100
00:07:53.950 --> 00:07:57.790
All that matters is
getting Robin outta here!

101
00:08:07.890 --> 00:08:09.800
[CHOPPER]
What're we gonna do?

102
00:08:12.460 --> 00:08:13.570
[ZORO]
It's too late now.

103
00:08:13.570 --> 00:08:16.940
Even if we wanted to, it's not like
we could go back and pick him up.

104
00:08:19.270 --> 00:08:21.240
I'm sure he'll figure out
something or other.

105
00:08:21.240 --> 00:08:23.950
[NAMI]
But the whole island
is swarming with Marines.

106
00:08:23.950 --> 00:08:25.420
He's not Luffy, after all.

107
00:08:25.420 --> 00:08:27.260
He can't fight them off on his own!

108
00:08:27.260 --> 00:08:29.460
[ZORO]
Even if we don't realize it at first,

109
00:08:29.460 --> 00:08:33.090
we've gotten stronger with
every challenge we've faced.

110
00:08:33.460 --> 00:08:37.600
You may not think he's tough,
but he's survived as well as anyone else.

111
00:08:37.600 --> 00:08:41.040
No one from our crew would
die at a time like this.

112
00:08:41.040 --> 00:08:41.910
Don't worry.

113
00:08:46.870 --> 00:08:49.170
Look! We're almost to the courthouse!

114
00:08:51.900 --> 00:08:53.270
[MARINE]
This oughta stop 'em.

115
00:09:00.380 --> 00:09:03.050
We've been hit! No!

116
00:09:03.050 --> 00:09:03.750
All right!

117
00:09:03.750 --> 00:09:05.180
We finally got one!

118
00:09:06.120 --> 00:09:09.290
[ZAMBAI]
Sodom!

119
00:09:11.270 --> 00:09:13.180
No. This is bad!

120
00:09:13.180 --> 00:09:14.610
He needs my help!

121
00:09:14.610 --> 00:09:16.860
[ZAMBAI]
Grit those teeth and hold on, Sodom!

122
00:09:16.860 --> 00:09:18.730
You can't fall yet!

123
00:09:19.830 --> 00:09:21.680
Guys, you're gonna have to jump!

124
00:09:21.680 --> 00:09:23.490
Get off him, quick!

125
00:09:23.490 --> 00:09:25.520
[ZAMBAI]
Sodom can't go on!

126
00:09:27.560 --> 00:09:29.430
That mortar hit him
square in the chest!

127
00:09:29.430 --> 00:09:31.390
He's about to go down!

128
00:09:31.390 --> 00:09:33.400
[ZAMBAI]
You gotta keep moving no matter what!

129
00:09:33.400 --> 00:09:35.500
You're the only ones who can do this!

130
00:09:47.640 --> 00:09:50.010
He says "go!"

131
00:10:03.260 --> 00:10:04.530
[MARINE]
He's coming down!

132
00:10:25.500 --> 00:10:26.570
[MARINE]
Nobody's riding it!

133
00:10:27.410 --> 00:10:29.440
Where'd they go?

134
00:10:30.610 --> 00:10:32.240
C'mon.

135
00:10:33.010 --> 00:10:35.050
[FAMILY MEN]
Let's go, Gomorrah!

136
00:10:37.240 --> 00:10:38.830
<b>Island Gate</b>

137
00:10:41.960 --> 00:10:44.360
[SOGEKING]
Why'd I have to not
land on that King Bull?

138
00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:46.740
What am I gonna do?

139
00:10:46.740 --> 00:10:48.710
I'm way behind everyone else now.

140
00:10:50.010 --> 00:10:54.780
[SOGEKING]
These shipwrights are awesome,
but I should probably catch up with the others.

141
00:10:54.780 --> 00:10:58.020
Then again, I did
leave the crew, didn't I?

142
00:10:58.020 --> 00:10:59.850
Maybe I should just run away.

143
00:11:06.830 --> 00:11:09.560
[SOGEKING]
No, running is the
last thing I should do!

144
00:11:09.560 --> 00:11:12.260
It doesn't matter whether
I'm a part of the crew or not.

145
00:11:12.260 --> 00:11:14.470
I put on this disguise so
I could help my friends.

146
00:11:14.470 --> 00:11:18.270
If Robin is willing to sacrifice herself
to save us, it's the least I can do!

147
00:11:18.270 --> 00:11:20.840
My manhood is on the line, here!

148
00:11:21.820 --> 00:11:25.420
All right, there's only one way to get
back to the others at this point.

149
00:11:25.420 --> 00:11:27.460
I call it "Operation Disguise Myself

150
00:11:27.460 --> 00:11:30.010
as One of the Government
Agents and Walk Straight

151
00:11:30.010 --> 00:11:32.540
to the Courthouse
Without Anyone Noticing."

152
00:11:32.540 --> 00:11:34.440
Okay, let's do this.

153
00:11:41.070 --> 00:11:43.410
Enemy attack! Enemy attack!

154
00:11:43.410 --> 00:11:44.440
They're flooding the island!

155
00:11:44.440 --> 00:11:45.850
We're all gonna sink!

156
00:11:47.630 --> 00:11:48.660
Huh?

157
00:11:50.730 --> 00:11:53.060
The giant woke up!

158
00:11:53.900 --> 00:11:56.840
[OIMO]
We tried for 50 years and blew it.

159
00:11:56.840 --> 00:11:58.570
We let our bosses down!

160
00:11:58.570 --> 00:12:00.370
[SOGEKING]
You mean the government?

161
00:12:00.940 --> 00:12:04.180
We're a disgrace to
all the giants in Elbaf!

162
00:12:06.030 --> 00:12:12.540
[SOGEKING]
Elbaf. Giants? Bosses? Wait a sec!

163
00:12:12.540 --> 00:12:14.270
Are you saying you're from Elbaf?

164
00:12:14.270 --> 00:12:17.310
Like, the Warrior's Village, Elbaf?

165
00:12:17.310 --> 00:12:19.480
Who the hell are you, runt?

166
00:12:20.180 --> 00:12:22.380
[SOGEKING]
I'm Sniper King from Sniper Island.

167
00:12:22.380 --> 00:12:25.690
I'm interested in your story,
by all means, continue!

168
00:12:26.880 --> 00:12:28.780
[SOGEKING]
Take your time.

169
00:12:28.780 --> 00:12:33.380
[OIMO]
There's not much point in telling
you, but I guess it can't hurt.

170
00:12:35.790 --> 00:12:38.920
Kashii and I used to
be pirates 100 years ago.

171
00:12:38.920 --> 00:12:41.290
Our crew traveled the whole world.

172
00:12:41.290 --> 00:12:44.960
But everything changed when
we visited a certain island.

173
00:12:45.590 --> 00:12:49.190
Since they couldn't come to an agreement,
our two bosses started a duel.

174
00:12:49.190 --> 00:12:50.690
[OIMO]
We had to split up the crew.

175
00:12:51.350 --> 00:12:52.850
We were at a loss.

176
00:12:52.850 --> 00:12:55.290
All we could do was go
back to our hometowns.

177
00:12:55.770 --> 00:12:58.740
A warrior's battle is
life-or-death but as soon as

178
00:12:58.740 --> 00:13:01.910
it's over the winner is supposed
to come back to their village.

179
00:13:01.910 --> 00:13:05.750
We waited for fifty years and
never heard from either of them.

180
00:13:05.750 --> 00:13:07.480
Something was wrong.

181
00:13:07.480 --> 00:13:10.960
So Kashii and I set out to
sea to go back to the island

182
00:13:10.960 --> 00:13:12.590
and find out what
happened with the duel.

183
00:13:13.330 --> 00:13:16.970
But on our way there, we got
captured by some Marines.

184
00:13:16.970 --> 00:13:17.840
They forced us to answer

185
00:13:17.840 --> 00:13:19.740
all kinds of questions about our crew.

186
00:13:19.740 --> 00:13:21.140
Then we found out the truth.

187
00:13:22.010 --> 00:13:26.350
Even though our bosses were strong fighters,
they got caught by Marines just like us

188
00:13:26.350 --> 00:13:28.860
and were stuck in
some big government jail!

189
00:13:28.860 --> 00:13:29.890
Huh?

190
00:13:29.890 --> 00:13:33.430
[OIMO]
All of that stuff happened
about 50 years ago.

191
00:13:33.880 --> 00:13:36.050
The government made a deal with us.

192
00:13:36.050 --> 00:13:40.400
They said if we would work for them for
100 years, they'd set our bosses free.

193
00:13:40.400 --> 00:13:44.080
All we had to do was protect
this gate from intruders.

194
00:13:44.080 --> 00:13:48.130
As long as we didn't let anyone through,
when our time was up, our bosses

195
00:13:48.130 --> 00:13:51.140
and us could all go
back to Elbaf together.

196
00:13:51.140 --> 00:13:55.210
Since giants live to be 300 or so,
we didn't think it was so bad.

197
00:13:55.210 --> 00:13:59.340
So we agreed to the deal and kept
our end of the bargain for 50 years.

198
00:13:59.340 --> 00:14:02.690
But then those pirates came through
the gate and ruined everything.

199
00:14:02.690 --> 00:14:04.390
That's why I'm so ashamed!

200
00:14:04.390 --> 00:14:05.680
That's why I'm crying!

201
00:14:05.680 --> 00:14:07.210
It's not fair.

202
00:14:07.210 --> 00:14:11.370
Now our bosses are gonna be stuck in that
dumb prison for the rest of their lives!

203
00:14:12.000 --> 00:14:14.270
[SOGEKING]
Hey, hold on, wait a second.

204
00:14:14.270 --> 00:14:15.970
There's something
funny about that story.

205
00:14:15.970 --> 00:14:18.140
[OIMO]
You think this is funny,
you little jerk!

206
00:14:18.140 --> 00:14:20.540
How dare you laugh at our pride?

207
00:14:20.540 --> 00:14:22.440
[USOPP]
I don't mean like funny "ha ha."

208
00:14:22.440 --> 00:14:24.240
I mean funny "weird."

209
00:14:24.240 --> 00:14:25.410
[OIMO]
And what's so weird about it?

210
00:14:25.410 --> 00:14:29.010
Before we came here, my crew
met those bosses of yours.

211
00:14:29.010 --> 00:14:31.440
And we saw them fighting their duel!

212
00:14:34.250 --> 00:14:36.310
Their names are
Dorry and Broggy, right?

213
00:14:36.310 --> 00:14:38.070
The warriors from Elbaf.

214
00:14:38.070 --> 00:14:43.580
Fighting in an evenly-matched duel,
over and over again, for 100 years!

215
00:14:47.350 --> 00:14:48.620
How?

216
00:14:48.620 --> 00:14:50.490
How do you know their names?

217
00:14:50.490 --> 00:14:52.220
You must be lying.

218
00:14:52.220 --> 00:14:55.590
If you need more proof than that,
I can tell you anything you want!

219
00:15:02.090 --> 00:15:02.790
And then...

220
00:15:15.340 --> 00:15:17.070
You still don't believe me?

221
00:15:17.070 --> 00:15:19.070
What do I have to tell you?

222
00:15:23.820 --> 00:15:25.990
Their weapons, maybe?

223
00:15:28.910 --> 00:15:30.080
How they fight?

224
00:15:30.820 --> 00:15:34.220
[BROGGY]
Seventy-three thousand, four
hundred and sixty-six duels.

225
00:15:34.220 --> 00:15:35.720
[USOPP]
I know everything about them!

226
00:15:35.720 --> 00:15:39.560
[DORRY]
Seventy-three thousand, four
hundred and sixty six draws.

227
00:15:39.560 --> 00:15:41.130
We really met them.

228
00:15:41.130 --> 00:15:42.700
I swear it!

229
00:15:49.370 --> 00:15:51.740
[USOPP]
They weren't captured 50 years ago.

230
00:15:51.740 --> 00:15:54.690
That's nothing but a big fat lie!

231
00:15:58.390 --> 00:16:05.610
<b>Courthouse</b>
<b>Rocketman</b>

232
00:16:18.270 --> 00:16:20.210
Wait, aim carefully!

233
00:16:20.770 --> 00:16:23.910
Get it in your sights, men!

234
00:16:23.910 --> 00:16:27.550
[ZAMBAI]
It's a trench mortar. Gomorrah! Dodge!

235
00:16:28.850 --> 00:16:31.150
Damn bastards had an
ambush waiting for us.

236
00:16:31.150 --> 00:16:33.550
Taking the main road
sure was a bad idea!

237
00:16:33.550 --> 00:16:35.650
Turn around, quick!

238
00:16:43.130 --> 00:16:44.770
Not so fast!

239
00:16:48.160 --> 00:16:49.770
[CHOPPER]
Sorry, Sodom.

240
00:16:49.770 --> 00:16:51.670
[MARINE]
Stop right there!

241
00:17:06.150 --> 00:17:07.650
[NAMI]
Chopper.

242
00:17:09.470 --> 00:17:10.740
Hm? Who could be calling?

243
00:17:10.740 --> 00:17:12.440
Yes? Hello?

244
00:17:13.210 --> 00:17:14.610
[KOKORO]
Howdy howdy!

245
00:17:14.610 --> 00:17:15.740
[FAMILY MAN (OVER SNAIL)]
Granny Kokoro!

246
00:17:15.740 --> 00:17:17.580
[FAMILY MAN (OVER SNAIL)]
What's going on?

247
00:17:18.080 --> 00:17:20.410
All right, sounds
like you're still alive.

248
00:17:20.410 --> 00:17:22.970
There's a little something
I forgot to tell you.

249
00:17:22.970 --> 00:17:25.680
[KOKORO (OVER SNAIL)]
Well, I'm sure you're busy,
so I'll make it quick.

250
00:17:25.680 --> 00:17:26.880
Listen carefully.

251
00:17:26.880 --> 00:17:30.150
If you remember that map Paulie drew,
you might notice there's no path

252
00:17:30.150 --> 00:17:32.520
from the courthouse to
the Gates of Justice.

253
00:17:32.520 --> 00:17:35.840
That's been bothering me but
I was afraid to ask about it.

254
00:17:35.840 --> 00:17:37.080
[KOKORO (OVER SNAIL)]
Look at the courthouse.

255
00:17:37.080 --> 00:17:39.490
You see those towers on either side?

256
00:17:39.490 --> 00:17:40.490
[NAMI]
Yeah, I see them.

257
00:17:40.490 --> 00:17:44.230
All right, now there's a lever on
the top floor of each of those towers.

258
00:17:44.230 --> 00:17:47.270
If you folks can get in
there and pull both of 'em,

259
00:17:47.270 --> 00:17:51.080
a drawbridge'll come down from the
courthouse to the Gates of Justice.

260
00:17:51.080 --> 00:17:52.180
Whoa!

261
00:17:52.180 --> 00:17:54.190
But how do you know
about all that stuff, Granny?

262
00:17:54.190 --> 00:17:57.760
[KOKORO (OVER SNAIL)]
I came here with Tom
ages ago to fix that bridge.

263
00:17:57.760 --> 00:18:00.180
Damn stupid ungrateful Government!

264
00:18:00.180 --> 00:18:01.970
Don't take it out on me!

265
00:18:01.970 --> 00:18:03.870
[KOKORO (OVER SNAIL)]
Chimney wants to talk, too.

266
00:18:03.870 --> 00:18:04.760
Pirate lady.

267
00:18:04.760 --> 00:18:07.140
Hey, can you hear me? Hello?

268
00:18:07.140 --> 00:18:09.040
[NAMI (OVER SNAIL)]
Yeah, I've got you loud and clear!

269
00:18:09.040 --> 00:18:10.110
[CHIMNEY (OVER SNAIL)]
Guess what?

270
00:18:10.110 --> 00:18:12.130
I just saw your rubber pirate buddy!

271
00:18:12.130 --> 00:18:15.180
He was over on the rooftop
of the courthouse just now!

272
00:18:15.180 --> 00:18:17.200
[GONBE (OVER SNAIL)]
Meow! Meow!

273
00:18:17.200 --> 00:18:18.400
So that's where he is!

274
00:18:18.400 --> 00:18:22.010
[CHIMNEY (OVER SNAIL)]
There was a bunch of smoke
and broken stuff up there too,

275
00:18:22.010 --> 00:18:24.140
so it looks like
he's wrecking the place!

276
00:18:24.140 --> 00:18:25.140
[NAMI]
Thanks!

277
00:18:25.140 --> 00:18:26.910
Hopefully we'll get there soon.

278
00:18:26.910 --> 00:18:30.820
[KOKORO (OVER SNAIL)]
And by the way, don't
hang up the transponder snail.

279
00:18:30.820 --> 00:18:33.390
I'd like to keep track of
what's goin' on with you folks.

280
00:18:33.390 --> 00:18:35.270
No problem. See ya!

281
00:18:36.070 --> 00:18:38.660
Can't keep the captain
waiting. Right, men?

282
00:18:38.660 --> 00:18:40.930
Gero! Gero!

283
00:18:40.930 --> 00:18:41.830
Good.

284
00:18:41.830 --> 00:18:43.080
You head straight for the courthouse.

285
00:18:43.080 --> 00:18:45.720
The sooner that your crew can
get back together, the better.

286
00:18:45.720 --> 00:18:46.920
That's what I say.

287
00:18:48.020 --> 00:18:50.480
Sounds good.

288
00:18:52.820 --> 00:18:56.620
Meanwhile, we'll split in two groups
and bring down the drawbridge.

289
00:18:57.960 --> 00:19:00.900
[ZAMBAI]
You hear that, Gomorrah?
To the courthouse!

290
00:19:10.740 --> 00:19:12.070
[ZAMBAI]
Gomorrah!

291
00:19:19.710 --> 00:19:22.170
[FAMILY MAN]
Damn. Who the hell is that?

292
00:19:27.650 --> 00:19:37.780
Tattoo: "Guilty"

293
00:19:34.200 --> 00:19:38.110
[GUILTY JUROR]
Don't get too cocky, scumbags.

294
00:19:41.810 --> 00:19:45.550
All right! The second one's down, too!

295
00:19:46.650 --> 00:19:47.750
[OFFICIAL]
How's that, huh?

296
00:19:47.750 --> 00:19:49.720
Not so fast now, are ya?

297
00:19:49.720 --> 00:19:51.220
[MARINE]
Everybody, move in!

298
00:19:51.220 --> 00:19:53.760
[ANNOUNCER]
Attention, all Marine guards.

299
00:19:53.760 --> 00:19:56.640
Here at Block D in
the southeast quadrant,

300
00:19:56.640 --> 00:19:59.350
the pirate's King Bull
has been eliminated!

301
00:19:59.680 --> 00:20:01.800
All units should move in immediately.

302
00:20:01.800 --> 00:20:04.100
Form a blockade around the entire area.

303
00:20:04.100 --> 00:20:05.100
I repeat!

304
00:20:05.100 --> 00:20:08.920
All military personnel
surround Block D now!

305
00:20:08.920 --> 00:20:12.700
[LEFT BASKERVILLE]
Seems that the jurymen have
delivered the verdict for us.

306
00:20:12.700 --> 00:20:15.440
[RIGHT BASKERVILLE]
And it's guilty as usual, huh?

307
00:20:17.450 --> 00:20:19.480
[LEFT & RIGHT BASKERVILLE]
Say something, man!

308
00:20:19.480 --> 00:20:20.250
[GUARDS]
Yes sir.

309
00:20:20.250 --> 00:20:22.150
[MARINE]
On our way!

310
00:20:21.320 --> 00:20:26.280
<b>Courthouse</b>

311
00:20:26.780 --> 00:20:29.560
The marines we trampled over
are catching up to us again.

312
00:20:29.560 --> 00:20:30.260
Not good.

313
00:20:30.260 --> 00:20:31.800
[ZAMBAI]
And it's not just them.

314
00:20:31.800 --> 00:20:33.370
We're surrounded here!

315
00:20:33.370 --> 00:20:36.570
[KIWI]
We've got trench
mortars aimed at us, too.

316
00:20:36.840 --> 00:20:40.170
There's gotta be like a million
bajillion of those guys out there!

317
00:20:40.170 --> 00:20:42.380
[CHOPPER]
We can't even run away anymore!

318
00:20:42.380 --> 00:20:44.160
What're we gonna do?

319
00:20:44.910 --> 00:20:49.440
<b>The Tower of Justice</b>

320
00:20:48.780 --> 00:20:50.450
[FRANKY]
Damn, you got it good.

321
00:20:50.450 --> 00:20:53.520
Not everyone gets
their own rescue squad.

322
00:20:53.820 --> 00:20:55.090
Well, just sayin'.

323
00:20:55.090 --> 00:20:58.220
It's not like I'm bitter 'cause
my men aren't coming to save me.

324
00:20:58.220 --> 00:21:00.960
They got better stuff to do, I'm sure.

325
00:21:18.310 --> 00:21:19.510
[SPANDAM]
Ah, that's right.

326
00:21:19.510 --> 00:21:21.050
I almost forgot.

327
00:21:21.050 --> 00:21:24.990
Before you leave, you
should take these with you.

328
00:21:29.060 --> 00:21:29.890
[JABURA]
Wait a sec!

329
00:21:29.890 --> 00:21:32.430
Those are Devil Fruits, aren't they?

330
00:21:34.280 --> 00:21:35.420
[KUMADORI]
Yoyoi.

331
00:21:36.010 --> 00:21:37.710
My!

332
00:21:38.870 --> 00:21:42.150
What a surprise!

333
00:21:42.150 --> 00:21:44.380
[FUKURO]
Chapapa.

334
00:21:44.380 --> 00:21:46.220
I've never seen one in person before!

335
00:21:46.220 --> 00:21:49.290
[KUMADORI]
It's my first time as well!

336
00:21:49.290 --> 00:21:50.090
[JABURA]
Stay away!

337
00:21:50.090 --> 00:21:52.560
Don't let those things near me!

338
00:21:52.560 --> 00:21:53.540
[KAKU]
You ate one, too.

339
00:21:53.540 --> 00:21:54.510
What's your problem?

340
00:21:54.510 --> 00:21:55.540
Why the fuss?

341
00:21:55.540 --> 00:21:56.280
[JABURA]
What?

342
00:21:56.280 --> 00:21:57.400
Haven't you heard?

343
00:21:57.400 --> 00:22:00.570
The reason they're called "Devil Fruits"
is because the people who eat them

344
00:22:00.570 --> 00:22:03.220
have a little devil living
inside their bodies!

345
00:22:03.220 --> 00:22:04.140
Just think.

346
00:22:04.140 --> 00:22:07.780
If I get too close to one of those things,
the devil inside me might pop out

347
00:22:07.780 --> 00:22:10.130
and start fighting with
the devil inside the fruit.

348
00:22:10.130 --> 00:22:13.200
If something like that happens,
my whole body'll be blown to bits!

349
00:22:13.930 --> 00:22:15.730
You're kidding me.

350
00:22:16.770 --> 00:22:18.170
That's nonsense.

351
00:22:18.170 --> 00:22:21.970
You're a member of an intelligence
agency and you believe that?

352
00:22:21.970 --> 00:22:23.340
What a shame.

353
00:22:23.340 --> 00:22:25.840
The condition for the
transfer of devil fruit powers

354
00:22:25.840 --> 00:22:29.770
has been confirmed by scientists on
the Grand Line for quite some time.

355
00:22:29.770 --> 00:22:34.380
The condition you're talking about only
happens when someone eats two Devil Fruits.

356
00:22:34.380 --> 00:22:37.910
I don't know if devils are involved,
but their bodies do burst apart.

357
00:22:37.910 --> 00:22:39.170
[LUCCI]
The price for greed.

358
00:22:39.170 --> 00:22:40.410
What fools.

359
00:22:40.410 --> 00:22:43.260
If you think about the risk that
comes with eating one fruit,

360
00:22:43.260 --> 00:22:45.300
you can only imagine
what kind of disaster

361
00:22:45.300 --> 00:22:48.370
you might bring upon
yourself by eating two of them.

362
00:22:48.900 --> 00:22:49.600
[JABURA]
Huh.

363
00:22:50.530 --> 00:22:52.490
So that's how it works. Still.

364
00:22:52.490 --> 00:22:53.360
I'm surprised.

365
00:22:53.360 --> 00:22:55.160
I can't believe you got two of these.

366
00:22:55.160 --> 00:22:56.790
Pretty impressive, Chief.

367
00:22:56.790 --> 00:22:58.190
How'd you pull that one?

368
00:22:58.190 --> 00:23:00.160
Let's just say I have connections.

369
00:23:00.160 --> 00:23:01.080
How's that?

370
00:23:01.080 --> 00:23:03.320
At any rate, best of luck.

371
00:23:03.790 --> 00:23:05.900
[SPANDAM]
That's right, CP9!

372
00:23:05.900 --> 00:23:08.490
Grow stronger and stronger!

373
00:23:08.490 --> 00:23:11.070
[SPANDAM]
As always, there is
a certain risk involved.

374
00:23:11.070 --> 00:23:14.210
We don't know what kind of
devils reside in those fruits.

375
00:23:14.210 --> 00:23:17.220
[KAKU]
I've never seen a fruit like
this in any reference book.

376
00:23:17.220 --> 00:23:21.450
You can feel a strange power coming
from them, a heaviness in the air.

377
00:23:21.450 --> 00:23:23.420
It's like they're
from a different world.

378
00:23:23.420 --> 00:23:26.090
[KALIFA]
That's what everyone says.

379
00:23:26.090 --> 00:23:30.190
I've been told that you only learn the name
of the fruit once you absorb its powers

380
00:23:30.190 --> 00:23:33.120
but there's no guessing what
kind of ability you'll gain.

381
00:23:33.120 --> 00:23:36.160
[KALIFA]
Well, there's no denying
that there's a risk involved.

382
00:23:36.160 --> 00:23:38.060
The wrong power could ruin your life.

383
00:23:38.060 --> 00:23:40.660
And either way, you'll
no longer be able to swim.

384
00:23:41.400 --> 00:23:45.190
[LUCCI]
It's not an issue of what power
you get, but how you use it.

385
00:23:45.190 --> 00:23:47.460
No matter what, you won't get weaker.

386
00:23:47.460 --> 00:23:50.950
And as for being unable to
swim, it's hardly a problem.

387
00:23:50.950 --> 00:23:52.050
It's a rare treasure.

388
00:23:52.050 --> 00:23:56.030
Of the thousands who search for them,
I'm sure most end up empty-handed

389
00:23:56.030 --> 00:23:58.640
or dead by the end of their journey.

390
00:23:58.640 --> 00:23:59.660
Just try it already.

391
00:23:59.660 --> 00:24:02.460
It'll be interesting.

392
00:24:02.460 --> 00:24:05.800
[JABURA]
Don't do it. Are you crazy?
That thing's evil!

393
00:24:05.800 --> 00:24:07.670
Also, they taste like crap, I tell you.

394
00:24:07.670 --> 00:24:08.600
Crap!

395
00:24:08.600 --> 00:24:10.470
Yeah right. He's jealous.

396
00:24:10.470 --> 00:24:13.110
He doesn't want them
getting stronger! Chapapa.

397
00:24:13.110 --> 00:24:13.840
Shame.

398
00:24:13.840 --> 00:24:17.650
You should know, Jabra, that envy

399
00:24:17.650 --> 00:24:21.960
and resentment are a man's downfall!

400
00:24:21.960 --> 00:24:23.740
[KUMADORI]
Yoyoi!

401
00:24:23.740 --> 00:24:25.910
Hey! Shut up!

402
00:24:26.660 --> 00:24:27.860
C'mon. Just stop.

403
00:24:27.860 --> 00:24:29.230
Think about this!

404
00:24:29.230 --> 00:24:31.780
If you sell these things,
you could make millions.

405
00:24:31.780 --> 00:24:34.850
But one bite and you'll be
cursed for the rest of your life!

406
00:24:39.320 --> 00:24:42.160
[FUKURO]
Chapapa.

407
00:24:43.260 --> 00:24:43.960
Yep.

408
00:24:43.960 --> 00:24:45.430
Interesting all right.

409
00:24:46.660 --> 00:24:47.600
Here goes.

410
00:24:47.600 --> 00:24:49.030
Hope it's good.

411
00:24:51.370 --> 00:24:52.340
[JABURA]
They ate them!

412
00:24:52.340 --> 00:24:53.300
No!

413
00:24:53.960 --> 00:24:55.320
[FUKURO]
Chapapa.

414
00:25:02.100 --> 00:25:04.200
What's wrong?

415
00:25:04.200 --> 00:25:05.270
[KUMADORI]
Yoyoi.

416
00:25:05.270 --> 00:25:10.100
Is your body besieged with
a strange metamorphosis?

417
00:25:10.100 --> 00:25:12.140
[FUKURO]
Chapapa!

418
00:25:19.650 --> 00:25:20.520
[BOTH]
Gross.

419
00:25:22.180 --> 00:25:23.250
[JABURA]
Say so sooner!

420
00:25:23.250 --> 00:25:24.320
[KALIFA]
It's really gross.

421
00:25:24.320 --> 00:25:25.320
Yeah, we got that!

422
00:25:25.320 --> 00:25:26.390
Chapapa!

423
00:25:26.390 --> 00:25:31.140
[KUMADORI]
And yet, you ate the
whole thing without a word!

424
00:25:31.140 --> 00:25:33.840
Well? C'mon!
Try doing something already.

425
00:25:33.840 --> 00:25:35.570
I wanna see what kind
of powers you got!

426
00:25:35.570 --> 00:25:39.600
[KALIFA]
I don't feel as if
anything is different.

427
00:25:39.600 --> 00:25:44.110
[LUCCI]
Soon you'll understand
the extent of your changes.

428
00:25:44.110 --> 00:25:47.030
The birth of new Devil Fruit
users is always exciting.

429
00:25:47.030 --> 00:25:51.330
Enjoy yourselves, but I'd try to
get those powers under control,

430
00:25:51.330 --> 00:25:52.450
while you still can.

431
00:25:52.450 --> 00:25:53.490
Depending on our orders,

432
00:25:54.270 --> 00:25:57.410
you might have to use
them in real combat soon.

433
00:25:57.410 --> 00:25:59.880
It seems Blueno couldn't wait.

434
00:25:59.880 --> 00:26:02.780
We'll have to see if
he saves any fun for us.

435
00:26:04.160 --> 00:26:08.630
<b>Courthouse</b>
<b>Rocketman</b>

436
00:26:04.210 --> 00:26:08.630
<b>Near the Island Gate</b>

437
00:26:13.740 --> 00:26:14.440
Hey.

438
00:26:14.440 --> 00:26:15.480
[MARINE]
Look!

439
00:26:19.750 --> 00:26:20.680
[MARINE]
All right.

440
00:26:20.680 --> 00:26:22.780
Oimo and Kashii are back on their feet!

441
00:26:23.880 --> 00:26:24.980
[PAULIE]
We're screwed.

442
00:26:27.050 --> 00:26:30.360
I don't have the strength to
fight these guys a second time.

443
00:26:32.960 --> 00:26:34.660
[TILESTONE]
We were so close!

444
00:26:37.760 --> 00:26:39.930
[WATCHDOG CAPTAIN]
Crush those criminals into the ground!

445
00:26:39.930 --> 00:26:43.420
Grind their little bones
between your toes, giants!

446
00:26:50.930 --> 00:26:53.900
[OIMO]
You bastards.

447
00:26:53.900 --> 00:26:57.640
How dare you?

448
00:27:01.240 --> 00:27:03.510
[OIMO & CASHY]
Lie to us!

449
00:27:08.920 --> 00:27:10.550
[WATCHDOG CAPTAIN]
What the hell?

450
00:27:10.550 --> 00:27:12.420
Don't tell me they betrayed us!

451
00:27:13.020 --> 00:27:18.360
[OIMO]
And now, with our bosses safe, before
we mourn all those years we wasted...

452
00:27:18.360 --> 00:27:23.200
[CASHY]
We're going let out every
last ounce of our anger on you!

453
00:27:23.200 --> 00:27:26.630
Are you ready, King of the snipers?

454
00:27:33.440 --> 00:27:35.310
[SOGEKING]
Let us not waste words.

455
00:27:35.310 --> 00:27:37.680
Hoist the signal for the counterattack!

456
00:27:37.680 --> 00:27:40.520
Soon we shall be
reunited with our comrades!

457
00:27:40.430 --> 00:27:45.180
<b>Courthouse</b>

458
00:27:40.430 --> 00:27:45.140
<b>Luffy vs. Blueno
Courthouse Rooftop</b>

459
00:27:53.030 --> 00:27:54.930
[BLUENO]
You're not bad.

460
00:27:56.040 --> 00:27:57.300
Not bad?

461
00:27:57.300 --> 00:28:00.540
[BLUENO]
I never thought he'd be able to
keep up with the speed of Shave.

462
00:28:00.540 --> 00:28:02.110
I'll have to watch that.

463
00:28:02.110 --> 00:28:05.480
And since he's made of rubber,
direct attacks won't work.

464
00:28:05.620 --> 00:28:06.870
[BLUENO]
Moon Walk!

465
00:28:09.580 --> 00:28:12.120
[LUFFY]
Now, Gum-Gum... [BLUENO]
Tempest Kick!

466
00:28:17.890 --> 00:28:19.390
[BLUENO]
Iron Body!

467
00:28:20.930 --> 00:28:22.800
Wheel!

468
00:28:32.640 --> 00:28:34.240
[BLUENO]
Door-Door!

469
00:28:38.780 --> 00:28:40.810
[LUFFY]
Was that a door on the ground?

470
00:28:40.810 --> 00:28:41.880
[BLUENO]
Door-Door.

471
00:28:43.570 --> 00:28:44.800
Whoa, wait a sec!

472
00:28:46.320 --> 00:28:48.760
Now there's a bunch of little
ones all over the place, too!

473
00:28:49.330 --> 00:28:50.960
Damn it, I can't move!

474
00:28:50.960 --> 00:28:54.300
This sucks. It's a stupid trap!

475
00:28:54.300 --> 00:28:55.900
You're the one doing this?

476
00:28:55.900 --> 00:28:57.940
But how? A Devil Fruit?

477
00:28:57.940 --> 00:29:00.420
[BLUENO]
The Door-Door Fruit, naturally.

478
00:29:00.420 --> 00:29:03.690
I turn all that I touch into doors.

479
00:29:07.790 --> 00:29:09.230
[BLUENO]
Revolving Door.

480
00:29:12.530 --> 00:29:13.460
Whoa, what?

481
00:29:13.460 --> 00:29:16.170
I'm not moving anywhere
but I'm spinning!

482
00:29:16.640 --> 00:29:18.210
I dunno which way is the front!

483
00:29:19.200 --> 00:29:20.740
Make it stop!

484
00:29:20.740 --> 00:29:22.150
[BLUENO]
Tempest Kick!

485
00:29:31.870 --> 00:29:33.340
Cook. See that?

486
00:29:33.340 --> 00:29:34.510
Yeah. I saw.

487
00:29:34.510 --> 00:29:35.680
You know what that means.

488
00:29:35.680 --> 00:29:37.810
Luffy's already fighting CP9.

489
00:29:37.810 --> 00:29:38.780
What?

490
00:29:38.780 --> 00:29:39.480
Huh?

491
00:29:39.680 --> 00:29:40.380
Seriously?

492
00:29:40.380 --> 00:29:41.210
Damn it.

493
00:29:41.210 --> 00:29:42.910
We're too late!

494
00:29:42.910 --> 00:29:44.250
But there's nothing we can do!

495
00:29:44.250 --> 00:29:45.520
We're totally surrounded.

496
00:29:45.520 --> 00:29:50.460
And after taking that last big hit,
I don't think Gomorrah's going anywhere!

497
00:29:50.460 --> 00:29:52.730
[OFFICIAL]
Everyone open fire and
shoot those pirates down

498
00:29:52.730 --> 00:29:55.400
from the monster
before it gets back up!

499
00:29:57.440 --> 00:29:58.400
Look. We gotta run.

500
00:29:59.240 --> 00:30:00.470
We can't wait here any longer.

501
00:30:00.470 --> 00:30:01.340
[SANJI]
Yeah.

502
00:30:01.340 --> 00:30:03.780
Let's cut through to the courthouse.

503
00:30:03.780 --> 00:30:06.280
[NAMI]
It's our only option.

504
00:30:06.910 --> 00:30:07.610
[FAMILY MAN]
Right! Let's go!

505
00:30:08.030 --> 00:30:09.630
Are you ready?

506
00:30:09.630 --> 00:30:10.880
[FAMILY MEN]
Yeah!

507
00:30:10.880 --> 00:30:15.520
[CHOPPER]
Wait. Nobody get off!

508
00:30:15.520 --> 00:30:17.080
What? Why?

509
00:30:20.760 --> 00:30:23.520
[CHOPPER]
Everyone, hold on tight!

510
00:30:39.320 --> 00:30:43.920
That... That's what Gomorrah says!

511
00:30:43.920 --> 00:30:45.120
[OFFICIAL]
It's still alive!

512
00:30:45.120 --> 00:30:46.790
[MARINE]
The monster's getting back up!

513
00:30:46.790 --> 00:30:47.830
[MARINE]
Fire!

514
00:30:47.830 --> 00:30:49.160
Stop it with the trench mortars!

515
00:30:49.160 --> 00:30:51.230
[MARINE]
Take that thing down!

516
00:30:51.230 --> 00:30:54.000
[FAMILY MAN]
Return fire! C'mon. Hurry!

517
00:31:00.610 --> 00:31:02.970
[ZAMBAI]
Go, Gomorrah! Charge!
